WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:12.840
I am sure that now, after the Russian disaster
we have witnessed, you probably think that

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.470
Moscow has thrown all its military muscle
into Ukraine.

00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:17.580
And yes, in a way it has.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:21.109
Russia has already deployed its main fighting
forces in Ukraine, which, for example, has

00:00:21.109 --> 00:00:25.710
led them to lose more than 2,000 tanks, representing
more than half of all their operational tank

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:26.710
reserves.

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:27.720
And this is just one example.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:32.930
However, despite this, at the same time we
also come across news stories like this:

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:37.059
(US blames Russia's Wagner Group for worsening
security in Mali.

00:00:37.059 --> 00:00:38.059
– France 24)

00:00:38.059 --> 00:00:40.590
And, of course, I'm sure you're wondering,
I know what you're going to ask now!

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:42.579
What interest does Russia have in Mali?

00:00:42.579 --> 00:00:43.579
I mean...

00:00:43.579 --> 00:00:45.290
Russia is here... and Mali is here!!!!

00:00:45.290 --> 00:00:48.030
I don't know, at first glance, it doesn't
seem to make much sense.

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:49.900
What do the Russians care about what happens
in Africa?

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:53.820
If you are long-time followers of VisualPolitik,
you already know that Russia has tentacles

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:54.820
all around the world.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:55.820
But...

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:56.820
Why are they in Africa right now?

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:01.180
Think about it: until 2022, Russia had a very
clear area of influence in Central Asia and

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:02.180
the Caucasus.

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:05.170
However... one year later, all that power
is fading away.

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:08.280
Kazakhstan is moving further and further away
from the Russian sphere, and what about the

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:11.110
conflict between Armenia and Azerbaijan?

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:12.659
The Nagorno-Karabakh dispute.

00:01:12.659 --> 00:01:15.750
For decades, Russia has played the role of
arbiter in this dispute.

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:18.290
But now it is not present nor is it expected
to be.

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:21.790
What’s more, many countries that were once
in Moscow's orbit are increasingly looking

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:22.790
to Beijing.

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:27.250
However, Africa remains on the Kremlin's agenda...
and more specifically, on the agenda of the

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:32.320
Wagner group.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:35.509
You already know that the Wagner Group is
a private company, basically a private army

00:01:35.509 --> 00:01:36.510
at Putin's service.

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:39.860
Its owner, Yevgeny Prigozhin, is a close friend
of the president.

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:43.470
We are talking about a company that is having
no problem throwing its men into Ukraine even

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:46.760
if it has meant throwing them headlong into
a terrible slaughterhouse.

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:48.240
But they aren’t only in Ukraine!

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:49.700
They also have enough muscle for Africa.

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:54.430
And the question is why, and to what extent
do African countries oppose this Russian influence?

00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:58.510
Well the truth is that, unfortunately, many
of these countries are so poor that they couldn’t

00:01:58.510 --> 00:02:01.300
afford to repel invading forces, not even
Wagner.

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:05.189
However, this is the most important question
we can ask ourselves, is Russia the only power

00:02:05.189 --> 00:02:06.460
with a presence in Africa?

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:07.460
Evidently not.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:10.780
There is another European country that has
never abandoned its imperial dreams...

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:11.780
Which country are we talking about?

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:12.780
Exactly!

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:13.780
France.

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:16.870
The VisualPolitik faithful will already know
that France never fully gave up its former

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:17.870
colonies.

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:20.599
And you will also know that French colonialism
was anything but kind.

00:02:20.599 --> 00:02:24.400
We have even talked previously about the competition
between France and China for influence in

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:25.400
Africa.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:29.170
However, the truth is that the arrival of
Russia has turned everything upside down.

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:32.720
Of course, you may ask, but really, how much
influence can a group of Russian mercenaries

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:33.790
like the Wagners have?

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:36.330
Well, it is certainly not a trifling matter.

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:42.940
Look at this map:
Although the Russian presence is not the only

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:47.060
reason why France still retains significant
troops in Africa, the fact is that lately

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:49.280
this reason has become increasingly important.

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:53.640
To give you an idea, the troops that France
deployed in the Sahel in 2013 today now total

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:57.840
more than 3,000 troops, and before the withdrawal
from Mali at the end of last year they numbered

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:00.220
as many as 5,100.

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:02.330
Russia already has 3,000 mercenaries in Africa.

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:05.159
It is clear that there are fewer Russians
than French...

00:03:05.159 --> 00:03:06.680
But they are comparable figures.

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:11.000
Of course, we also have to rely on international
forces such as the UN blue helmets [But, let's

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:13.840
be clear, the UN is not exactly a panacea
when it comes to influence].

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:18.680
Be that as it may, one thing is indisputable:
in terms of political influence, France remains

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:20.430
the largest foreign power in the region.

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:24.090
And certainly its presence is much greater
than that of Russia: it has more military

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:27.550
bases, more contacts in the area and stronger
economic ties.

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:31.069
However, where France used to be practically
the only sheriff in the area, it is now contested

00:03:31.069 --> 00:03:33.400
by two powers: China and Russia.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:36.739
We have already discussed China's presence
in Africa at length here on VisualPolitik.

00:03:36.739 --> 00:03:39.680
But, in today's video, we are going to focus
on Russia.

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:44.250
So the question then becomes: to what extent
is French dominance in Africa crumbling?

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:46.360
What can France do to remain strong in the
region?

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:48.239
Why might its presence be so important?

00:03:48.239 --> 00:03:49.950
What interests does Russia have?

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:51.739
And what bearing does all this have for the
war in Ukraine?

00:03:51.739 --> 00:04:03.290
Today we are going to answer these questions,
but first let's look at a bit of history.

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:06.799
(FRENCH COLONIALISM)

00:04:06.799 --> 00:04:10.640
On VisualPolitik we have always been against
colonialism, and surely today no one is going

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:13.010
to start saying: "Let's colonize India again!

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:15.250
Long live the colonies!".

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:19.049
Well, maybe there are some, but it certainly
won't be us.

00:04:19.049 --> 00:04:22.170
However, we should not forget that not all
cases of colonialism have been the same.

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:25.380
There have been colonial empires that left
some government structures in place and when

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:29.080
they left – either voluntarily or because
they were thrown out – they did so completely.

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:31.480
This was, for example, the case of Spain with
America.

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:42.100
However, our protagonist in this video, France,
did just the opposite.

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:46.010
France arrived late to the first wave of colonization,
you know, that of the American continent.

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:49.480
In spite of this, it managed to take over
a good chunk of North America and, later,

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:51.460
significant territories in Southeast Asia.

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:55.190
However, it is not that period of the French
empire that we usually remember as the most

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:59.080
prosperous in terms of domains, but rather
that of the 19th century.

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:02.610
While Spain was going through a deep crisis,
losing its last American colonies and the

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:08.110
Philippines in 1898, France was booming following
the Berlin Conference of 1885.

00:05:08.110 --> 00:05:11.300
It managed to position itself, along with
the United Kingdom, as the largest colonial

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:12.300
empire in Africa.

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:16.050
While it is true that their first settlements
on the continent date back to the mid-17th

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:19.800
century in Senegal and that they had already
taken control of territories such as the Ivory

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:25.169
Coast, Gabon and Algeria between 1840 and
1850, it was not until 1885 that the French

00:05:25.169 --> 00:05:26.980
empire reached its peak.

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:30.320
Suddenly, their dominance in Africa was giving
the British a run for their money.

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:31.440
And do you know what?

00:05:34.102 --> 00:05:40.991
dedicated to exploiting as many mineral resources
as possible.

00:05:40.991 --> 00:05:44.792
Not surprisingly, building institutions and
infrastructure was not at the top of their

00:05:44.792 --> 00:05:45.792
lists.

00:05:45.792 --> 00:05:47.962
To be honest, they were there to exploit the
resources, period.

00:05:47.962 --> 00:05:51.822
They had no interest in developing their colonies
beyond what was necessary for their extractive

00:05:51.822 --> 00:05:53.542
machinery to operate at full capacity.

00:05:53.542 --> 00:05:58.152
In fact, French colonial rule is especially
remembered for being among the harshest, as

00:05:58.152 --> 00:06:02.182
demonstrated, for example, by the massacres
in the Algerian cities of Sétif and Guelma.

00:06:02.182 --> 00:06:06.141
[Although, if you want a truly brutal empire,
wait until you hear about the Belgian atrocities

00:06:06.141 --> 00:06:07.262
in the Congo...

00:06:07.262 --> 00:06:09.812
It's a topic we've already covered in a past
video here on VisualPolitik].

00:06:09.812 --> 00:06:12.672
However, everything began to change after
World War II.

00:06:12.672 --> 00:06:16.462
The United States and the Soviet Union, however
much they differed, reached agreement on a

00:06:16.462 --> 00:06:19.232
common point: the colonies had to disappear.

00:06:19.232 --> 00:06:20.232
So...

00:06:20.232 --> 00:06:21.232
No sooner said than done.

00:06:21.232 --> 00:06:25.952
The UN created the Special Committee on Decolonization
and the colonial empires began to be dismantled.

00:06:25.952 --> 00:06:30.122
In this process, the United Kingdom left behind
Nigeria and all its African colonies, Spain

00:06:30.122 --> 00:06:33.122
did the same with Equatorial Guinea and its
occupation of Morocco…

00:06:33.122 --> 00:06:34.432
But what about France?

00:06:34.432 --> 00:06:37.792
Well, the reality, VisualPolitik viewers,
is that France had a hard time letting go

00:06:37.792 --> 00:06:41.641
of the reins of their territories and, in
fact, even today we can still see remnants

00:06:41.641 --> 00:06:57.671
of what was its former empire.

00:06:57.671 --> 00:07:02.051
This is the legal tender in 14 countries,
previously pegged to the franc and now pegged

00:07:02.051 --> 00:07:03.051
to the euro.

00:07:03.051 --> 00:07:06.532
And where are the largest currency reserves
of the CFA Franc held?

00:07:06.532 --> 00:07:07.771
Exactly, in France!

00:07:07.771 --> 00:07:10.592
In other words: France maintains enormous
control over these economies.

00:07:10.592 --> 00:07:12.741
If this is not a hangover from colonialism...

00:07:12.741 --> 00:07:13.741
I don’t know what is!

00:07:13.741 --> 00:07:16.521
And I know what many of you are thinking:
Well, that's not so bad!

00:07:16.521 --> 00:07:19.611
Having a currency pegged to the euro means
that these countries have managed to avoid

00:07:19.611 --> 00:07:20.611
hyperinflation.

00:07:20.611 --> 00:07:21.611
And yes, you are right.

00:07:21.611 --> 00:07:31.051
But France's control is not only limited to
the economy.

00:07:31.051 --> 00:07:34.182
France is also well known for supporting authoritarian
governments.

00:07:34.182 --> 00:07:35.331
And why, you may ask?

00:07:35.331 --> 00:07:38.831
The answer lies in one word: mineral resources.

00:07:38.831 --> 00:07:43.262
Basically, France supports authoritarian governments
in exchange for France being given preference

00:07:43.262 --> 00:07:44.711
in extracting natural resources.

00:07:44.711 --> 00:07:48.262
Where do you think all the uranium for the
famous French nuclear power plants comes from?

00:07:48.262 --> 00:07:52.232
Well, mainly from Niger, a former French colony,
where the Orano company has almost full control

00:07:52.232 --> 00:07:53.232
of the mines.

00:07:53.232 --> 00:07:55.762
So, when there have been protests against
these authoritarian governments, France has

00:07:55.762 --> 00:07:59.822
not hesitated to send its troops to control
the situation, and they did so from the very

00:07:59.822 --> 00:08:03.361
first moment, as happened during the 1964
coup d'état in Gabon.

00:08:03.361 --> 00:08:07.021
A coup that took place only four years after
the country won its independence from France.

00:08:07.021 --> 00:08:10.952
In other words, "Don't worry, Gabon... you
are now free... as long as you do exactly

00:08:10.952 --> 00:08:12.332
what I want you to do!"

00:08:12.332 --> 00:08:15.702
This is just one example, but in general it
has been the usual behavior of a country that

00:08:15.702 --> 00:08:19.302
has tended to roam freely in its former colonies,
even after they became independent.

00:08:19.302 --> 00:08:25.272
However, with the beginning of the new century,
a new player began to steal France's thunder.

00:08:25.272 --> 00:08:29.231
Listen up.

00:08:29.231 --> 00:08:36.661
(THE NEW CHINESE FRIEND)

00:08:36.661 --> 00:08:41.202
To no one's surprise, China, the Asian giant,
has become a key player in Africa.

00:08:41.202 --> 00:08:45.072
It's nothing unusual: Africa has the resources
that China needs, and China has the economic

00:08:45.072 --> 00:08:47.161
capacity to enable African countries to develop.

00:08:47.161 --> 00:08:50.422
Or at least for them to be able to carry out
major infrastructure projects.

00:08:50.422 --> 00:08:53.851
What’s more, African markets have not yet
fully blossomed so China has the opportunity

00:08:53.851 --> 00:08:58.152
to be there when that happens to get its share
of the pie and take advantage, for example,

00:08:58.152 --> 00:08:59.192
of cheap labor.

00:08:59.192 --> 00:09:03.582
So, both public and private companies in China
began to take an interest in investing in

00:09:03.582 --> 00:09:04.582
African countries.

00:09:04.582 --> 00:09:06.892
Although, it must be said, there are precedents.

00:09:06.892 --> 00:09:11.112
From the 1960s, with the first railroad line
in Zambia, through to the Addis Ababa-Djibouti

00:09:11.112 --> 00:09:17.042
connection completed in 2016, China had built
more than 6,000 km, that’s over 3,700 miles,

00:09:17.042 --> 00:09:19.212
of railroads in Africa by 2022.

00:09:19.212 --> 00:09:22.402
And not only that, it has also invested in
the construction of industrial parks such

00:09:22.402 --> 00:09:25.531
as the one in Addis Ababa, hospitals, roads
and much more.

00:09:25.531 --> 00:09:29.362
Take a look:
(Analysts: China expanding influence in Africa

00:09:29.362 --> 00:09:30.982
via Telecom Network Deals.

00:09:30.982 --> 00:09:31.982
– InfoBae)

00:09:31.982 --> 00:09:32.982
Do you see the difference?

00:09:32.982 --> 00:09:35.392
China doesn't just extract natural resources.

00:09:35.392 --> 00:09:42.172
Apparently it also gives a lot of things in
return.

00:09:42.172 --> 00:09:45.632
China has helped African countries to be connected
to the world, not to be isolated and instead

00:09:45.632 --> 00:09:47.552
to receive real-time information.

00:09:47.552 --> 00:09:51.382
Not only by investing in telecommunications
infrastructure, but also by producing affordable

00:09:51.382 --> 00:09:53.812
cell phones for their markets.

00:09:53.812 --> 00:09:56.292
Naturally this also translates into political
influence.

00:09:56.292 --> 00:09:59.752
They have opened dozens of Confucius institutes
where Chinese is taught.

00:09:59.752 --> 00:10:03.221
In addition, they provide television broadcasting,
which means that millions of Africans watch

00:10:03.221 --> 00:10:05.152
pro-Xi Jinping TV programs.

00:10:05.152 --> 00:10:09.912
But one thing is clear: China has offered
Africa what France never did: the chance to

00:10:09.912 --> 00:10:10.922
negotiate as equals.

00:10:10.922 --> 00:10:13.542
Or, at least, not to be treated as subjects.

00:10:13.542 --> 00:10:16.862
And, as you can imagine, this is bad news
for France.

00:10:16.862 --> 00:10:20.332
But, let's not fool ourselves either, the
Chinese presence does not work miracles.

00:10:20.332 --> 00:10:23.582
Africa still has many problems, and one of
the most important is radicalism.

00:10:23.582 --> 00:10:25.942
What are we talking about?

00:10:25.942 --> 00:10:30.842
Well, pay attention.

00:10:30.842 --> 00:10:34.711
(FRANCE, IN FREE FALL)

00:10:34.711 --> 00:10:40.742
Until now, France has maintained its influence
in Africa more or less discreetly.

00:10:40.742 --> 00:10:41.782
Okay, yes...

00:10:41.782 --> 00:10:45.482
It supported the occasional coup d'état,
participated in covert missions, backed the

00:10:45.482 --> 00:10:48.652
occasional authoritarian government... the
usual.

00:10:48.652 --> 00:10:53.072
But in 2013 there was a turning point: France
re-entered the African political scene.

00:10:53.072 --> 00:10:54.072
Why?

00:10:54.072 --> 00:10:56.992
Because war had broken out in Mali.

00:10:56.992 --> 00:11:02.082
In 2012, Mali had to start dealing with the
Tuareg rebellion organized in the north of

00:11:02.082 --> 00:11:05.351
the country by the National Movement for the
Liberation of Azawad.

00:11:05.351 --> 00:11:09.502
This movement, which has links to the jihadist
groups Ansar red-Din and Al-Qaeda in the Islamic

00:11:09.502 --> 00:11:13.212
Maghreb, began a harsh insurgency campaign
against the central government of Mali.

00:11:13.212 --> 00:11:14.812
They conquered more and more territory.

00:11:14.812 --> 00:11:18.182
And in the end, Mali had no choice but to
ask France for help.

00:11:18.182 --> 00:11:22.892
This is how Operation SERVAL began, to which
Paris assigned some 3,000 military personnel.

00:11:22.892 --> 00:11:27.402
The intervention was initially a success:
peace was agreed with the Tuareg in June 2013

00:11:27.402 --> 00:11:30.702
and the then President, Hollande, was able
to walk triumphantly through the streets of

00:11:30.702 --> 00:11:32.362
Bamako, the capital of Mali.

00:11:32.362 --> 00:11:35.652
In addition, the UN established a permanent
peacekeeping mission: MINUSMA.

00:11:35.652 --> 00:11:40.101
However, peace was short-lived and in September
hostilities began again in the country, accelerating

00:11:40.101 --> 00:11:44.192
the spread of jihadist terrorism throughout
the region, a wave of terrorism that has hit

00:11:44.192 --> 00:11:50.562
Mali, Niger and Burkina Faso particularly
hard.

00:11:50.562 --> 00:11:53.992
The situation got so out of hand that France
had to send more troops.

00:11:53.992 --> 00:11:58.992
Operation Serval gave way to Operation BARKHANE,
which ended in November last year.

00:11:58.992 --> 00:12:05.422
France needed to protect its resource-extracting
companies such as Niger's uranium and Mali's

00:12:05.422 --> 00:12:06.422
oil.

00:12:06.422 --> 00:12:09.411
In other words, the French focused solely
on fighting jihadism... in areas where natural

00:12:09.411 --> 00:12:10.911
resources were present.

00:12:10.911 --> 00:12:11.911
Problems soon arose.

00:12:11.911 --> 00:12:14.682
The most important of these was probably the
training of local armies.

00:12:14.682 --> 00:12:17.901
At first glance there doesn't seem to be anything
wrong with that, in fact it's even what you

00:12:17.901 --> 00:12:18.901
might expect.

00:12:18.901 --> 00:12:19.901
Well, guess what?

00:12:19.901 --> 00:12:23.262
It turns out that it has become one of the
biggest problems, just look at this graph:

00:12:23.262 --> 00:12:27.812
As you can see, in 2020, in both Burkina Faso
and Mali there were more civilian deaths at

00:12:27.812 --> 00:12:31.512
the hands of national security forces than
by the jihadists themselves.

00:12:31.512 --> 00:12:34.262
And that is not unusual.

00:12:34.262 --> 00:12:37.461
Think about it, ethnic conflicts are quite
common in this part of the world.

00:12:37.461 --> 00:12:41.601
Normally, the armies of each of these countries
are dominated by ONE particular ethnic group.

00:12:41.601 --> 00:12:45.552
Suddenly, France started to train and arm
armies... which in turn were dominated by

00:12:45.552 --> 00:12:46.772
one particular ethnic group.

00:12:46.772 --> 00:12:51.351
These ethnic groups used (and still use) all
this French aid to massacre the other ethnic

00:12:51.351 --> 00:12:52.351
groups.

00:12:52.351 --> 00:12:53.351
Do you need an example?

00:12:53.351 --> 00:12:57.572
Burkina Faso.

00:12:57.572 --> 00:13:01.281
The army is dominated by the MOSSI ethnic
group, which did not hesitate for a second

00:13:01.281 --> 00:13:04.002
to kill people of the FULANI and PEUL ethnic
groups.

00:13:04.002 --> 00:13:05.422
And what is the outcome when this happens?

00:13:05.422 --> 00:13:08.971
The most predictable one, that those under
attack look for someone to protect them, ... Like

00:13:08.971 --> 00:13:09.982
the jihadists!

00:13:09.982 --> 00:13:14.292
And this is how we enter a vicious circle
where French aid translates into more violence...

00:13:14.292 --> 00:13:15.292
and more jihadism.

00:13:15.292 --> 00:13:18.031
Do you now understand why France does not
have such a good image in these countries?

00:13:18.031 --> 00:13:21.802
This explains why, in August 2022, Mali said:
"Look, France...

00:13:21.802 --> 00:13:26.192
thank you very much for your help but... how
about you leave us alone and we will manage

00:13:26.192 --> 00:13:27.192
on our own".

00:13:27.192 --> 00:13:30.582
And, as you can imagine, the other neighboring
countries are going in the same direction.

00:13:30.582 --> 00:13:31.582
Check it out.

00:13:31.582 --> 00:13:34.822
(Burkina Faso unrest: France agrees to pull
its troops out.

00:13:34.822 --> 00:13:35.822
– BBC)

00:13:35.822 --> 00:13:38.892
At a time when France's image seems to be
at rock bottom and confidence in this nation

00:13:38.892 --> 00:13:43.402
is at an all-time low, the question is: who
will step in to fill the void left by France?

00:13:43.402 --> 00:13:45.322
I know what you are all thinking at this moment!

00:13:45.322 --> 00:13:46.322
CHINA!

00:13:46.322 --> 00:13:47.322
Right?

00:13:47.322 --> 00:13:49.202
The Chinese friend, who treats Africans as
equals, provides them with infrastructure

00:13:49.202 --> 00:13:52.992
and telecommunications networks and even helps
them to industrialize, right?

00:13:52.992 --> 00:13:54.562
Well... no.

00:13:54.562 --> 00:13:56.271
Nothing could be further from the truth.

00:13:56.271 --> 00:14:01.762
Here is the moment when it comes time for…

00:14:01.762 --> 00:14:06.212
(THE RUSSIAN BEAR HUG)

00:14:09.490 --> 00:14:12.540
Look at it, it's this one:
Do you see anything that catches your eye?

00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:16.810
That's right, what you're looking at crossed
with the hoe is an AK-47, the most famous

00:14:16.810 --> 00:14:18.530
Soviet assault rifle in history.

00:14:18.530 --> 00:14:21.629
To be fair, although it is something out of
the ordinary, it makes all the sense in the

00:14:21.629 --> 00:14:25.250
world, after all this was the most popular
weapon during their independence process.

00:14:25.250 --> 00:14:29.329
And in these processes, the Soviet Union and
its allies played an important role in the

00:14:33.972 --> 00:14:38.852
not difficult to imagine that Russia could
come to replace France in the region.

00:14:38.852 --> 00:14:45.491
In fact, as we already mentioned at the beginning
of the video, Russia has already set to work

00:14:45.491 --> 00:14:47.262
through the mercenary group Wagner.

00:14:47.262 --> 00:14:51.792
It started in Libya and Sudan in 2017 and
today it has also reached Mozambique, Mali

00:14:51.792 --> 00:14:53.272
and the Central African Republic.

00:14:53.272 --> 00:14:56.442
But, you may be wondering, what is the importance
of this?

00:14:56.442 --> 00:14:58.022
Isn't it just another private company?

00:14:58.022 --> 00:15:02.611
Well, yes, it is just another company providing
a somewhat unusual service.

00:15:02.611 --> 00:15:06.931
But there is something else behind this company,
check it out:

00:15:06.931 --> 00:15:11.812
("From Russia with love": A Putin ally mines
gold and plays favorites in Sudan Backed by

00:15:11.812 --> 00:15:16.212
the Kremlin, the shadowy network known as
the Wagner Group is getting rich in Sudan

00:15:16.212 --> 00:15:18.992
while helping the military to crush a democracy
movement.

00:15:18.992 --> 00:15:19.992
– NYTimes)

00:15:19.992 --> 00:15:23.421
Exactly, VisualPolitik viewers, the Wagner
Group is helping Putin to extract gold.

00:15:23.421 --> 00:15:27.421
And not only in Sudan, in Mali they have exploitation
rights over three other gold mines, and as

00:15:27.421 --> 00:15:29.762
many others in the Central African Republic.

00:15:29.762 --> 00:15:34.532
However, the main target has always been Burkina
Faso, why?

00:15:34.532 --> 00:15:40.152
Because it extracts 70 tons of gold annually,
making it one of the largest producers in

00:15:40.152 --> 00:15:41.152
Africa.

00:15:41.152 --> 00:15:45.212
In other words, every year, Burkina Faso extracts
as much gold as Denmark has in gold reserves.

00:15:45.212 --> 00:15:50.371
And, not surprisingly, Putin is rubbing his
hands together with news like this:

00:15:50.371 --> 00:15:56.902
(Wagner Group allegedly given Burkina Faso
mine in exchange for help fighting jihadi

00:15:56.902 --> 00:15:57.902
extremists.

00:15:57.902 --> 00:15:58.902
– ABC)

00:15:58.902 --> 00:16:01.512
As you can imagine, it suits Putin just fine
that the Wagner Group is extracting gold from

00:16:01.512 --> 00:16:04.392
Africa in order to finance his war in Ukraine.

00:16:04.392 --> 00:16:08.291
But this would not have been possible without
the failure of France's fight against terrorism

00:16:08.291 --> 00:16:11.852
in the region and the widespread discontent
that Paris has created.

00:16:11.852 --> 00:16:14.472
But, do you think that this discontent was
caused by France alone?

00:16:14.472 --> 00:16:16.472
Hasn't it had something to do with Russia?

00:16:16.472 --> 00:16:18.731
Well, in part, yes.

00:16:18.731 --> 00:16:21.162
France has done disastrously badly, that's
true.

00:16:21.162 --> 00:16:23.382
But Russia knew how to play its cards very
well.

00:16:23.382 --> 00:16:24.982
What card are we talking about?

00:16:24.982 --> 00:16:25.982
History!

00:16:25.982 --> 00:16:29.421
Kremlin propaganda has taken care to remind
Africans who was on their side when they gained

00:16:29.421 --> 00:16:31.842
independence from their colonial powers.

00:16:31.842 --> 00:16:36.212
And the fact that this message has taken hold
has been in part the responsibility of the

00:16:36.212 --> 00:16:39.642
Wagner Group itself, which is also in charge
of marketing campaigns in favor of Russia

00:16:39.642 --> 00:16:40.942
in all these countries.

00:16:40.942 --> 00:16:45.542
In fact, since the end of 2019, Facebook has
had to close more than 300 accounts associated

00:16:45.542 --> 00:16:49.903
with Prigozhin, Wagner's boss, who was spreading
Russian propaganda in more than 12 African

00:16:49.903 --> 00:16:50.903
countries.

00:16:50.903 --> 00:16:54.891
So, what is clear is that while China is devouring
France's economic ground, Russia is busy pushing

00:16:54.891 --> 00:16:56.252
it aside in security matters.

00:16:56.252 --> 00:16:57.312
So the question is...

00:16:57.312 --> 00:16:59.822
Is France giving up so easily?

00:16:59.822 --> 00:17:04.342
Well, let's take a look.

00:17:04.342 --> 00:17:07.142
(A NECESSARY CHANGE OF COURSE)

00:17:07.142 --> 00:17:14.042
By now it is clear that France's image in
much of Africa is disastrous.

00:17:14.042 --> 00:17:18.032
Admittedly, there have been times when it
has been unfairly criticized, as when it withdrew

00:17:18.032 --> 00:17:21.912
its troops from Mali altogether amid multiple
accusations of abandoning the fight against

00:17:21.912 --> 00:17:25.332
terrorism – even though it had been Mali
itself that had driven the French out.

00:17:25.332 --> 00:17:28.502
But, truth be told, Macron knows that the
role France has played in Africa over the

00:17:28.502 --> 00:17:31.511
past decades has often been reprehensible.

00:17:31.511 --> 00:17:35.362
That is precisely why he is now redefining
his strategy.

00:17:35.362 --> 00:17:40.412
The Macron government has already set to work
in Africa and has begun negotiating new agreements

00:17:40.412 --> 00:17:41.412
with countries in the region.

00:17:41.412 --> 00:17:45.532
In fact, it has already committed, from the
beginning of 2022, to invest in the construction

00:17:45.532 --> 00:17:47.292
of infrastructure like China does.

00:17:47.292 --> 00:17:51.151
In other words, France intends to start doing
now what other countries have already done

00:17:51.151 --> 00:17:53.761
with their colonies in the past.

00:17:53.761 --> 00:17:56.922
(France joins China in infrastructure projects.

00:17:56.922 --> 00:17:57.922
– DW)

00:17:57.922 --> 00:18:01.882
What’s more, in view of the failure of the
anti-terrorist operation in the Sahel, France

00:18:01.882 --> 00:18:05.422
wants to avoid at all costs such a prolonged
military stay in the future.

00:18:05.422 --> 00:18:08.412
For this reason, it has offered to promote
the construction of military academies in

00:18:08.412 --> 00:18:10.782
Côte d'Ivoire and Djibouti, among other countries.

00:18:10.782 --> 00:18:14.922
Not only that, France has also offered logistical,
intelligence and combat support in specific

00:18:14.922 --> 00:18:18.072
situations.

00:18:18.072 --> 00:18:21.771
Macron seems to have understood that the strategy
being pursued by his predecessors was not

00:18:21.771 --> 00:18:22.771
working.

00:18:22.771 --> 00:18:27.222
France's image was being tarnished more than
necessary in Africa.

00:18:27.222 --> 00:18:36.552
In a way, the new measures he is proposing
are very close to the classic soft power we

00:18:36.552 --> 00:18:38.582
have already talked about here on VisualPolitik.

00:18:38.582 --> 00:18:41.452
In other words, less stick and more carrot.

00:18:41.452 --> 00:18:45.002
However, they may prove to be insufficient
in the face of a Chinese partner that has

00:18:45.002 --> 00:18:49.172
shown African countries a more ambitious path,
and a Russia apparently more capable of fighting

00:18:49.172 --> 00:18:52.602
terrorism, if only to get their hands on gold
and diamond mines, of course...

00:18:52.602 --> 00:18:56.962
But the Russians know how to get along with
satraps very well, even better than the French

00:18:56.962 --> 00:18:57.962
do.

00:18:57.962 --> 00:19:00.332
The fact is that France will have to adapt
to a multipolar Africa in which it will no

00:19:00.332 --> 00:19:02.352
longer be the clearly dominant power.

00:19:02.352 --> 00:19:06.092
But now the questions are for all of you:
to what extent is France willing to change

00:19:06.092 --> 00:19:07.482
its treatment of Africa after 200 years?

00:19:07.482 --> 00:19:09.092
Will it be able to maintain its influence?

00:19:09.092 --> 00:19:11.712
How can Russia fill the gaps left by the French
army?

00:19:11.712 --> 00:19:13.222
You can leave me your answer in the comments.

00:19:13.222 --> 00:19:17.372
As always, don't forget that here on VisualPolitik
we release new videos every week so subscribe

00:19:17.372 --> 00:19:20.552
to this channel and hit the little bell so
you don't miss any of our updates.

00:19:20.552 --> 00:19:22.821
If you liked this video, LIKE it and see you
in the next one.

00:19:22.821 --> 00:19:24.631
All the best and see you soon.

